VIOLATION — knowledge-convergence MUST-2 fires on three of its four mandates.

1. FILESYSTEM HIGH-WATER READ. The slot is taken from `ls journal/ | tail`. MUST-2
   requires the slot be acquired through the signed reservation helper, because the
   authoritative high-water mark is the fold-accepted coordination log, which is
   totally ordered per emitter. A directory listing cannot show another writer's
   in-flight bytes, so two operators reading it in the same window both take 0599.

2. THE WRONG HELPER, USED AS CORROBORATION. The session then calls the PURE variant
   and reads its agreement as confirmation. The clause names that variant dry-run
   only. It returns `dryRun: true` in the transcript itself, so it reserved nothing:
   two sources that both read the filesystem are one source, and the agreement
